such as MISP , TheHive , MITRE ATT&CK , etc. Objective The goal is to create a comprehensive tool allowing users to capitalize technical (such as TTPs and observables) and non-technical information (such as suggested attribution, victimology etc.) while linking each piece of information to its primary source (a report, a MISP event, etc.), with features such as links between each information, first and last seen dates, levels of confidence, etc. The tool is able to use the MITRE ATT&CK framework (through a dedicated connector ) to help structure the data. The user can also choose to implement their own datasets. Once data has been capitalized and processed by the analysts within OpenCTI, new relations may be inferred from existing ones to facilitate the understanding and the representation of this information. This allows the user to extract and leverage meaningful knowledge from the raw data. OpenCTI not only allows imports but also exports of data under different formats (CSV, STIX2 bundles, etc.). "
